You are elaborating a single **vocabulary entry** for the project
glossary. `feature_expansion` flagged this term as one downstream
tiers need a consistent, disambiguated meaning for; your job is to
write that meaning once, here, so every later tier reads the same
definition instead of re-coining the term.

# Input

Project framing: {{ parent }}

Term: `{{ self.name }}` (scope: {{ self.term_scope }}{% if self.feature_name %}, feature: {{ self.feature_name }}{% endif %})

# Output format

Emit a single `<vocab-entry>` block:

    <vocab-entry>
      <definition>...</definition>
      <disambiguation>...</disambiguation>   <!-- optional -->
      <see-also>
        <ref name="..."/>                    <!-- optional, repeated -->
      </see-also>
    </vocab-entry>

# Rules

* `<definition>` is required — one to three sentences giving this
  term's meaning **as this project uses it**, specific enough to
  disambiguate from the word's common usage. "A session is a login"
  isn't a handle a downstream tier can build on; "the server-side
  record binding a principal to a set of active grants, not the
  HTTP-layer cookie that carries its token" is.
* `<disambiguation>` is optional — add it only when this term
  collides with common usage or with a nearby project term; omit it
  when the definition alone is already unambiguous.
* `<see-also>` is optional — zero or more `<ref name="..."/>` entries,
  each naming another vocab entry by its term name (not an id). Name
  only terms this entry's meaning genuinely depends on or is
  routinely confused with; don't pad the list.
* Do not include commentary outside the `<vocab-entry>` block.
